@startuml direct-rialto-request-lifecycle-state
title Lifecycle of one needData request: stage, claim, answer
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> NoRequest

NoRequest --> Pending : OnNeedData() with gate NONE\n(hasPending = true)
NoRequest --> NoRequest : OnNeedData() while gated\nrejected: answered at once, never staged

Pending --> Pending : Complete() adds a segment,\ncount < frameCount and morePending

Pending --> Claimed : Complete() batch full or !morePending -> OK\nComplete() with EOS latched -> EOS\nOnNoSpace() -> OK (or NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES if empty)\nDropSample() -> EOS or NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES\nUnblock() / WaitFor*() abort -> NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES\nnew OnNeedData() supersedes -> NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES\nSignalEos() / SetGate(false) -> EOS

Pending --> NoRequest : OnCancelNeedData()\n(Rialto cancelled: no haveData)
Pending --> NoRequest : Reset()\n(new session: dropped silently)

Claimed --> NoRequest : caller sends haveData(status, requestId)\nafter the handshake lock is released

note right of Claimed
  A claim clears hasPending and snapshots the BatchSummary
  inside one critical section, so exactly one thread
  owns the duty to answer.  There is no timer: a Pending
  request stays open until one of the events above happens.
end note
@enduml
